0
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Settings
// Switch and basic rules.
//   Event enabled: 1 turns the event on, 0 off.
//   Minimum guild members: Members a guild needs to take the castle.
//   How the winner is decided: 0 Guild holding the castle at the end | 1 Most total time holding it | 2 Longest single hold
//   Event map: Map where the event takes place.
//   Castle NPC: Monster number of the castle NPC that players must stand next to.
//   NPC direction: Way the NPC faces (0 to 7).
//   NPC X: Position X of the NPC.
//   NPC Y: Position Y of the NPC.
//   Kills raise PK level: 1 makes a kill inside the event area raise the PK level of the killer, 0 makes it free.
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~1]      [1~80]        [0~2]    [0~200]    [0~1999]    [0~7]        [0~254]    [0~254]    [0~1]
//  Enabled    MinMembers    Style    Map        NPC         Direction    X          Y          IncreasePK
//--------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    1          1             1        2          380         1            225        237        0
end

1
//----------------------------------------------------------
// Event Zones
// Areas of the event (a rectangle each). The respawn area must be bigger than one cell. The PvP zone is optional: with no PvP zone the whole event area is PvP.
//   Zone: 0 Event Area | 1 Respawn Area | 2 PvP Zone
//   Left side: Left side of the area.
//   Top side: Top side of the area.
//   Right side: Right side of the area.
//   Bottom side: Bottom side of the area.
//----------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~2]    [0~254]    [0~254]    [0~254]    [0~254]
//  Zone     StartX     StartY     EndX       EndY
//----------------------------------------------------------
    0        193        188        255        255        //Event Area
    1        200        190        244        200        //Respawn Area
    2        210        208        244        240        //PvP Zone
end

2
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Timing
// The times and rules of one event.
//   Warning before start (minutes): Minutes before the start that everyone is warned (1 to 59).
//   Duration (minutes): Minutes the event lasts.
//   Who can take the castle: 1 Guild master only | 2 Assistant or higher | 3 Battle master or higher | 4 Any guild member
//   Time to take the castle (seconds): Seconds the player must stand at the NPC, without moving or dying, to take the castle (1 to 255).
//   End early at (minutes): Minutes of total holding after which the event ends and that guild wins. * never ends early. Only used with the style 1 and 2.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [1~59]       [Number]     [Number]           [1~255]            [Number]
//  AlarmTime    EventTime    OccupationRange    OccupationDelay    OccupationMaxTime
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    5            2            4                  5                  1
end

3
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Schedule
// When the event starts. The second is not used: it starts on the minute.
//   Year: The year when the event starts. * means every year.
//   Month: The month when the event starts. * means every month.
//   Day: The day of the month when the event starts. * means every day of the month.
//   Day of the week: -1 Every day | 1 Sunday | 2 Monday | 3 Tuesday | 4 Wednesday | 5 Thursday | 6 Friday | 7 Saturday
//   Hour: The hour when the event starts. * means every hour.
//   Minute: The minute when the event starts. * means every minute.
//   Second: The second when the event starts. * means every second.
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [*/1970~9999]    [*/1~12]    [*/1~31]    [*/1~7]      [*/0~23]    [*/0~59]    [*/0~59]
//  Year             Month       Day         DayOfWeek    Hour        Minute      Second
//----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    *                *           *           4            22          00          0           //
    *                *           *           7            22          00          0           //
end

4
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Winner Guild Reward
// Prize for every member of the winner guild.
//   WCoin C: WCoin C given to each member of the winner guild. 0 gives none.
//   WCoin P: WCoin P given to each member of the winner guild. 0 gives none.
//   Goblin Points: Goblin Points given to each member of the winner guild. 0 gives none.
//   Ruud: Ruud given to each member of the winner guild. 0 gives none.
//   Item Bag: Item bag dropped for each member of the winner guild. * gives none.
//   Buff: Effect (Effect.txt) given as a buff. * or 0 gives none.
//   Buff time (minutes): Minutes the buff lasts (the server multiplies it by 60, so the value is in minutes, not seconds).
//   Buff value 1: First power value of the buff (see the effect).
//   Buff value 2: Second power value of the buff (see the effect).
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [Number]    [Number]    [Number]    [Number]    [Number]
//  WC               WP               GP               Ruuds            ItemBag     Buff        BuffTime    Val1        Val2
//------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    9                0                0                0                *           *           0           0           0
end

5
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Conquest Rewards
// Prizes for the players who held the castle the most (conquest ranking).
//   Position: Position of the player in the conquest ranking (1 is the best).
//   WCoin C: WCoin C given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   WCoin P: WCoin P given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   Goblin Points: Goblin Points given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   Ruud: Ruud given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   Item Bag: Item bag dropped for that player. * gives none.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [1~100]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [Number]
//  Top        WC               WP               GP               Ruuds            ItemBag
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    1          8                0                0                0                *
end

6
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
// Kill Ranking Rewards
// Prizes for the players with the most kills (kill ranking).
//   Position: Position of the player in the kill ranking (1 is the best).
//   WCoin C: WCoin C given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   WCoin P: WCoin P given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   Goblin Points: Goblin Points given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   Ruud: Ruud given to that player. 0 gives none.
//   Item Bag: Item bag dropped for that player. * gives none.
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//  [1~100]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [0~999999999]    [Number]
//  Top        WC               WP               GP               Ruuds            ItemBag
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
    1          8                0                0                0                *
end

7
//-----------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
//	Kill Points
//----------------------------------------------------------
// Kill Points
// Points a kill gives, by the rank of the player killed in his guild.
//   Killed player's rank: 1 Guild Master | 2 Assistant Guild Master | 3 Battle Master | 4 Member
//   Points: Points the killer gets for killing a player of that rank.
//----------------------------------------------------------
//  Range    Points
//----------------------------------------------------------
    1        10
    2        8
    3        8
    4        5
end